1. b12x and RoCEnante (Local Inference Lab / FlashInfer)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Repository: https://github.com/local-inference-lab/b12x
Upstream integration: https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/tree/main/flashinfer/experimental/b12x
Authors: Luke Alonso (@lukealonso / @lukea), @original-el8 (@el8), and contributors
License: Apache License, Version 2.0

Attribution:
- "RoCEnante" (b12x.comm.roce, documented in b12x's docs/rocenante.md) is the
  name and one-shot RoCEv2 collective architecture created by the b12x authors
  for multi-node DGX Spark tensor parallelism. SparkFlash's one-shot RDMA
  collective transport (crates/sparkflash-comm, kernels/rocenante_oneshot_sm121.cuh,
  kernels/rocenante_oneshot_sm121.cu, and crates/sparkflash-kernels/src/roce_*.rs)
  adopts the RoCEnante name and design: ping-pong pinned unified-memory staging
  and receive slots registered across dual ConnectX-7 RoCEv2 rails, GPU-side
  staging with a system-scope fence, a dedicated CPU proxy polling a sequence
  doorbell and striping RDMA writes across rails with per-rail sequence arrival
  flags, and deterministic canonical rank-order (0 + 1 + 2 + 3) f32 reduction
  with a single round-to-nearest-even bf16 store.
- The "b12x_*" kernel naming prefix (kernels/b12x_*.cu) and the "spark_b12x_*"
  32x32 weight micro-tile / UE8M0 block-scale indexing helpers
  (kernels/m4_common_sm121.cuh, crates/sparkflash-kernels/src/mxfp8_ref.rs,
  crates/sparkflash-kernels/src/mxfp4_ref.rs, and
  crates/sparkflash-kernels/tests/b12x_index_parity.rs) are named after and
  inspired by b12x's SM120/SM121 block-scaled MXFP8/MXFP4/NVFP4 kernel and
  direct-I/O loader architecture.
- The SM120/SM121 mma.sync / ldmatrix / cp.async GEMM tiling shared by
  kernels/opt_mma_sm121.cu, kernels/opt_mma_common_sm121.cuh and
  kernels/opt_mma_bf16_sm121.cuh draws on prior art from b12x's SM120/SM121
  block-scaled GEMM kernels.
- In crates/sparkflash-model-qwen4-exp (kernels/qwen4_exp_sm121.cu,
  kernels/qwen4_prefill_sm121.cu, src/ple.rs, src/checkpoint.rs, src/device.rs,
  src/device/prefill.rs, src/device/blocks.rs) and kernels/quant_decode_sm121.cuh,
  the SM120/SM121 NVFP4/FP8 decode kernels, asynchronous CUDA driver dispatch,
  and out-of-core safetensors Per-Layer Embedding (PLE) shard paging with
  POSIX_FADV_RANDOM and parallel pread draw on prior art from b12x
  (b12x/loader/_ple_reader.c and SM120/SM121 MoE/attention kernels).
- The pre-converted per-rank weight files (the shared container,
  crates/sparkflash-weights/src/rank_file.rs; DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash's index and
  arena loader, crates/sparkflash-device/src/converted.rs; GLM-5.3-Flash's,
  crates/sparkflash-model-glm5-next/src/convert.rs) and their bounded parallel
  O_DIRECT reads into host and device memory (read_file_parallel_into_slice and
  Cuda::upload_file_parallel in crates/sparkflash-kernels/src/cuda_driver.rs)
  draw on prior art from b12x's direct-I/O loader (b12x/loader/_direct.c).

