2. NVIDIA Flare (flare-local-inference / spark-local-inference)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Repository: https://github.com/NVIDIA/flare-local-inference
Authors: NVIDIA Corporation & Affiliates, Luke Alonso (@lukealonso / @lukea),
         @original-el8 (@el8), @voipmonitor, @eugr, and contributors
License: Apache License, Version 2.0

Attribution:
- Flare (Helios Rust runtime and Ignition compiler, built on b12x and FlashInfer)
  pioneered native Rust local inference serving on SM120/SM121 and multi-node
  DGX Spark hardware.
- SparkFlash draws architectural inspiration from Flare across several subsystems:
  * Rust integration of the RoCEnante dual-rail one-shot RDMA collective model
    (helios/native/roce_proxy.c, helios/src/execution/roce.rs);
  * Bounded O_DIRECT and io_uring asynchronous NVMe row gathering and caching
    for out-of-core Engram / PLE embedding tables
    (helios/src/engram/reader.rs -> crates/sparkflash-engram);
  * Pre-converted per-rank weight artifacts for fast cold boot without Python or
    JIT warmup overhead (crates/sparkflash-weights/src/rank_file.rs and the
    per-model converters in section 1);
  * Stateless seeded Gumbel-max sampling so draft and target steps share
    identical random draws without host RNG state synchronization;
  * Online calibrated acceptance profiles paired with a step cost model for
    adaptive speculative verification depth
    (helios/src/scheduler/speculation.rs, cost.rs, learning.rs ->
    crates/sparkflash-scheduler, crates/sparkflash-model/src/speculation.rs);
  * SM120/SM121 mma.sync tensor-core GEMM tiling in the shared MMA headers
    (kernels/opt_mma_common_sm121.cuh, kernels/opt_mma_bf16_sm121.cuh) that the
    DeepSeek kernels and the Qwen4-Exp prefill image both include.

