- https://github.com/z-lab/dflash (Copyright (c) 2026 Z Lab, MIT License)
- https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang (Copyright 2023-2024 SGLang Team,
  Apache License, Version 2.0)
Papers & posts:
- Jian Chen, Yesheng Liang, Zhijian Liu. "DFlash: Block Diffusion for Flash
  Speculative Decoding." International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML),
  2026.
- Inco AI. "DFlash 2: Keep Drafting Parallel." August 2026.
  https://inco.ai/blog/dflash2/

Attribution:
- Block-diffusion speculative drafting (one parallel draft block of a bonus
  token plus mask positions, conditioned on hidden states captured from the
  target model and verified by the target in one pass) is the DFlash method of
  Chen, Liang and Liu, with its reference implementation in z-lab/dflash.
- The DFlash 2 drafter served by crates/sparkflash-model-qwen4-exp (its
  configuration in crates/sparkflash-model/src/dflash2.rs, src/device/dflash.rs
  and the q4d_* kernels in kernels/dflash2_sm121.cu) follows
  Inco AI's DFlash 2 release for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: the five-layer non-causal
  sliding-window drafter, the per-block grouped causal convolutions around
  attention and MLP, the low-rank candidate path selector over the target head's
  top candidates, and the target-layer feature capture (layers 5/15/25/35/45,
  the mean of the four hyper-connection streams) described by the model card
  and its capture patch. The drafter weights are Inco AI's and are loaded, not
  redistributed.
- Inco AI's GLM-5.3-Flash drafter is the same architecture at GLM-5.3-Flash's
  geometry (4,096 wide, target layers 5/14/24/33/42), served by the same drafter
  code on crates/sparkflash-model-glm5-next's tensor-parallel ranks
  (src/device.rs): every rank runs it whole, scores its blocks with its own
  slice of the target head, and the ranks merge their candidates. Its target
  rows are the mean of the four hyper-connection streams of each target
  layer's finished rows, as SGLang's GLM-5.3-Flash DFlash capture
  (python/sglang/srt/models/glm5_next.py) takes them.
  crates/sparkflash-model/src/dflash2.rs parses its configuration and checks it
  against the GLM-5.3-Flash pack's. Its weights are licensed CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 for
  research and evaluation; they are loaded from the user's own copy and are
  neither redistributed nor modified here, and commercial use needs a license
  from Inco AI.
- The drafter forward, the selector walk and the verify/accept protocol were
  implemented by reading SGLang's DFlash support (python/sglang/srt/models/
  dflash.py, python/sglang/srt/speculative/dflash_*.py and python/sglang/kernels/
  ops/speculative/dflash.py, which SGLang notes it adapted from the DFlash
  reference implementation). No SGLang or DFlash source is copied; the Rust and
  CUDA code is an independent implementation of the same arithmetic.

