Attribution:
- The Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration architecture planned in
  crates/sparkflash-model-glm5-next (45-layer 3:1 hybrid of Kimi Delta
  Attention linear attention and DeepSeek Sparse Attention with a 4-token
  k-pool indexer, 4-stream manifold-constrained hyper-connections, 288-expert
  top-8 sigmoid MoE with one shared expert, and one MTP layer) follows Z.ai's
  GLM-5.3-Flash release and its reference implementation in Transformers
  (src/transformers/models/glm5_next), which was read for the arithmetic; no
  Transformers source is copied.
- Kimi Delta Attention (the per-channel forget gate and the delta-rule state
  update) is the method of the Kimi Linear paper, whose kernels the Transformers
  implementation takes from FLA. DeepSeek Sparse Attention and its lightning
  indexer are DeepSeek-V3.2's; the cross-layer index sharing the configuration
  can name is IndexCache's. The hyper-connections are mHC, run through the host
  reference shared with DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (crates/sparkflash-weights/src/mhc.rs,
  section 6).
- The MTP layer (an eh_proj over the normed embedding of a token and the normed
  hidden the model left at the position before it, then one DSA + MoE layer
  without hyper-connections, the head norm and the shared LM head) is
  DeepSeek-V3's multi-token prediction module as Z.ai's release ships it. The
  speculative decoding that drafts with it and verifies the drafts in one step
  (crates/sparkflash-model-glm5-next/src/device.rs) is an independent
  implementation.
- The block-scaled FP8 layout of the official release (FP8 E4M3 codes with one
  FP32 weight_scale_inv per 128x128 tile, quant_method fp8 with dynamic
  activations) is the format the Transformers fine-grained FP8 integration
  reads; its planner (TensorPlan::push_fp8_block) and scale grid
  (linalg::ScaleGrid::Tile) in crates/sparkflash-weights are an independent
  implementation, shared with the Qwen3.8 pack's MTP experts, as is the decode
  GEMV that multiplies it (q4e_gemv_tiled_e4m3_block, in the Qwen3.8 pack's
  tiled GEMV, with the activations quantised per 128 columns as the host's
  quant::quantize_activation_fp8_tiles does, which takes vLLM's
  per-token-group quantiser's answer for an all-zero tile: zero codes and a
  zero scale). The tensor plan's byte totals are pinned to both Z.ai releases' model.safetensors.index.json
  files.
- The device arm (crates/sparkflash-model-glm5-next/src/device.rs) decodes
  through the Qwen3.8 pack's token cubin, whose GLM-5.3-Flash section (the mHC
  mixers, the clamped SwiGLU, the noaux router, the k-pool indexer's key norm,
  pooling, scores and pick, and the routed experts' FP8 GEMV) is an independent
  implementation of the arithmetic of the host reference above; no Transformers
  or FLA source is copied.
- The released configuration carried under
  crates/sparkflash-model-glm5-next/config/ is Z.ai's config.json from
  zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash, MIT License.
